    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>By 370 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> had reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a>; their conquest of the Alans and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goths">Goths</a> drove thousands of Goths to seek refuge across the Lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> in 376.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a>, sole ruler from 445, the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> agreed in 449 to pay an annual tribute of 2,100 pounds of gold; in 451 he invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and in 452 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</li><li>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila</a> died in 453 the Gepid king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardaric">Ardaric</a>'s Germanic coalition defeated his sons at the Battle of Nedao, and the last king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dengizich">Dengizich</a> was killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a> in 469.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Only three words of the Hunnic language are recorded, all apparently Indo-European; everything else known of it comes from personal and tribal names, so the language is held by many to be unclassifiable.</p></aside>
    </section>

